# Ignore-file for website/Dockerfile. BuildKit reads `<dockerfile>.dockerignore`
# next to the Dockerfile in preference to the context root's `.dockerignore`,
# which is what lets this live beside the only image the repo builds instead of
# at the repo root.
#
# PATTERNS ARE STILL RELATIVE TO THE BUILD CONTEXT — the repository root, not
# website/ — because website/public/assets is a symlink to assets/ (see the
# Dockerfile header). Deny everything, then re-admit the two directories the
# build needs; otherwise the Swift sources and the ~1GB GhosttyKit.xcframework
# ride along.
*
!website/
!assets/

# Regenerated inside the image by `bun run build` — never copy a host build in.
website/node_modules/
website/public/docs/
website/public/tailwind.css
website/public/sitemap.xml
website/public/robots.txt

website/Dockerfile
website/Dockerfile.dockerignore
**/.DS_Store
